     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEESAC in cooperation with the Western Balkans authorities and covering the period 2012-2016 is to further deepen the research and go beyond the quantitative data in order to shed light on how the widespread availability of small arms shape the demand for it and to obtain a better understanding of the factors and mechanisms which fuel demand and shape risk-taking behaviors involving firearms, including those related to criminality.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEESAC developed the Methodology for the Research of the factors fuelling demand and misuse of firearms in the Western Balkans and published Terms of Reference for the service of conducting Research on factors shaping demand and misuse of small arms and ammunition in the Western Balkans. The objective of the Research Expert ToR is to engage a qualified individual expert to 1) ensure quality assurance by providing relevant inputs for the overall regional research on factors fueling demand and misuse of firearms in the Western Balkans, 2) develop a desk review and systematic literature review, and 3) assist development of the instruments for the overall research. Once the research is finished, the expert shall also 4) compile the results from the comprehensive research and provide a synthesis report with practical recommendations to inform prevention and reduction measures, identifying both risk and protective factors that influence demand for firearms.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
